1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
TEN (ENVELOPE)

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[narrator] Ten:

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
The ability to envelop your body
in a shroud of Nen aura,

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
making it tougher
and slowing the effects of aging.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
ZETSU (SUPPRESS)

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Zetsu:

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
A technique which shuts off
your flow of Nen aura.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Effective for concealing your presence
and recovering from fatigue.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,000
REN (REFINE)

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Ren:

11
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
A technique for creating
an especially strong Nen aura.

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
It is crucial for increasing your power.

13
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:28,000
HATSU (RELEASE)

14
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Hatsu:

15
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The release of your Nen aura,
after using Ren to boost it.

16
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
These four elements
are known as the Four Exercises

17
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
and are critical to the mastery of Nen.

18
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
FOUR EXERCISES

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
[theme song playing]

20
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Gon.

21
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
You and me, we’ve got to learn
all that we can about Nen.

22
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Yeah!

23
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
AN x EMPTY x THREAT

24
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
[narrator] After two months during which
Gon was forbidden to practice Nen,

25
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Wing summoned Gon and Killua
to his room for a meeting.

26
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[Wing] Gon, Killua.

27
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Starting today, you will be
training alongside Zushi.

28
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
And Gon, splendid work.

29
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
I’m happy to see
that you kept your promise.

30
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
It’s because of your promise thread.

31
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
There were a couple of times
I got really close to giving in.

32
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
But then I’d look at the thread,

33
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
and I could feel myself getting calmer.

34
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Because I imbued it with Nen to help you.

35
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Wait… Really?

36
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
No. I was kidding.

37
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,000
[Gon] Uh...

38
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Hold on.

39
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
How can you tell
Gon’s been keeping his promise?

40
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
As far as you know,

41
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
he was secretly cheating this whole time.

42
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Because the promise thread
is completely intact.

43
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Gon. I know it’s been a while,

44
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
but would you show me your Ten?

45
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
-You sure?
-Yes.

46
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Oh, man…
Do I even remember how?

47
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
It's been so long.

48
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
I wonder if I can still pull it off.

49
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
[Wing] What do you think, Zushi?

50
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
It-- It’s amazing!

51
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
His aura is flowing completely
around him, sir!

52
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,000
It’s soft and tranquil…

53
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
but it’s-- it’s so powerful, too!

54
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
That’s it!

55
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
What a relief!

56
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
I was worried that
I had forgotten how to do it.

57
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Once you’ve learned the technique,
it can’t be forgotten.

58
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
However, in order to become a true master,

59
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
you will have to practice diligently.

60
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
But it felt a lot easier
than it did before

61
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
and I haven’t practiced Ten
in a real long time.

62
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
I can explain.

63
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
That’s because you’ve been
training your spirit every day.

64
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Now please look at your left hand.

65
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
What?

66
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,000
It broke!

67
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
I tied the thread to your finger
with my own Nen,

68
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
so if you had broken your promise,

69
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
the thread would’ve broken as well.

70
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
[Killua] You can do stuff like that?

71
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Question, Mister Wing:

72
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
You saw Hisoka and Kastro’s match?

73
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
[Wing] Yes, I did.

74
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
So, what was Hisoka’s ability?

75
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Do you think we could do that?

76
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Send our limbs flying all over the place?

77
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
[Wing] Hmm...That's a difficult question.

78
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Gon. Have you seen
a recording of the fight?

79
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
No. Not yet, sir.

80
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Then I’ll explain while we watch.

81
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,000
[audience cheering]

82
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
[Wing] There.

83
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
See the strands of aura extending out
from his left hand?

84
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
[Gon] “Strands of aura”?

85
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Yes.

86
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Do you see them?

87
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,000
[Killua grunts, focusing]

88
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
No… I don’t think so…

89
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
I can’t see anything…

90
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Me neither, sir.

91
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
[focusing grunt, focusing grumble]

92
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
[Gon] Are there really strands of aura
coming out of his left hand?

93
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Are you sure?

94
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
I am.

95
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
See, Hisoka is using a technique

96
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
that makes his aura exceedingly difficult
to perceive.

97
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,000
SUPPRESS

98
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
It’s a high-level application of Zetsu,
known as “In”.

99
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
CONCEAL

100
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
It renders even powerful aura
invisible to your opponent.

101
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,000
And to counter this,

102
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
you must focus all of your Ren
in both of your eyes,

103
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
utilizing a technique known as Gyo.

104
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,000
GYO (FOCUS)

105
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:55,000
The method Gon used
in his fight with Gido

106
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
might also be useful.

107
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
But you can’t counterattack,

108
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
so you’d ultimately get yourself killed.

109
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Right…

110
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
[Wing] My assignment for the two of you
is to practice Ren,

111
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
until you can see through Hisoka’s In.

112
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
But Master…

113
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
What about me?

114
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
What kind of training should I do?

115
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Zushi.

116
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
You should already be just strong enough
to see past Hisoka’s In.

117
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
You think so?

118
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
[Wing] If you would,
please show them your Ren.

119
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
[determined grunt]

120
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,000
O-- Osu!

121
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,000
[focusing exhale]

122
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
[shouts] Ren!

123
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,000
It's so strong.

124
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
It’s just as big as ours…

125
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
but the aura is so much more dense!

126
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Now focus that aura into your eyes.

127
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
[Zushi] Osu!

128
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
[focusing effort]

129
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
And Gyo!

130
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Good.

131
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
So, tell me, can you see the aura
rushing from his body?

132
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
[straining]

133
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Yes.

134
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
There are individual strands of aura.

135
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
How many of them do you see?

136
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Twelve… Wait.

137
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
No. I think I count 13, sir.

138
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Not quite.

139
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
But you are very close indeed.

140
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,000
[tired exhale, panting]

141
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
I really could see them!

142
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
You’re really making
excellent progress, Zushi.

143
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Osu! Thank you! I’m trying, Master.

144
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:43,000
By channeling every ounce
of your power through Gyo,

145
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:47,000
you achieved a level where you could see
through Hisoka’s In.

146
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
But with enough training,

147
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,000
you’ll be able to use Gyo
even while you’re fighting.

148
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Now do you understand?

149
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
First, practice using Ren

150
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
and master the application known as Gyo.

151
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Then and only then

152
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,000
will you discover
the true nature of Hisoka’s ability.

153
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
You asked if you would ever be able
to use that same ability.

154
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
And my answer is yes,
but at the same time, no.

155
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,000
[both] Huh?

156
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Regardless of what his power is,

157
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,000
so long as it uses Nen,
you’ll be able to learn it.

158
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
But it’s important to note
that Nen abilities

159
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
depend on the individual.

160
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Because of course, we each possess
different specialties and preferences

161
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
which means that Nen differs
for each person.

162
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
If you’re serious about mastering Nen,

163
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
you shouldn’t merely copy
the abilities of others.

164
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
You need to first identify
your own particular strengths.

165
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Strengths, huh?

166
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,000
[Wing] You’re still growing,

167
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
so you haven’t settled on one form yet.

168
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,000
My advice is to enrich yourself
as much as possible.

169
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
That is the purpose of your training.

170
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Train with all of your might.

171
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Play just as hard.

172
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
And enjoy life!

173
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
[Zushi, Gon and Killua] Osu!

174
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,000
I believe the last day of Killua’s window
to compete is June ninth.

175
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
And Gon, yours is the tenth, correct?

176
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Both of you should register to fight
on your final day.

177
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
In the meantime, you'll train.

178
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
You must both learn Gyo
before you enter battle.

179
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,000
[Gon, Killua and Zushi] Osu!

180
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
[Gon] Hey, Zushi!

181
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Your Ren was impressive!

182
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:29,000
You got way ahead of us
while I was stuck recuperating.

183
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
No. I’ve still got a long way to go.

184
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Hey! Why don’t we practice a little.

185
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
It should be fun!

186
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Okay. Then let’s go up to your room, Gon.

187
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Mm hm.

188
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Zushi. Killua.

189
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
I feel it.

190
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
We’ve got company, guys.

191
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
[elevator dings]

192
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
You don’t give up, do you?

193
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
That isn’t the way to make friends.

194
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Now, that’ll be enough of that.

195
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Just tell us when you’re going to fight,

196
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
because I’m dying to be your opponent.
[light chuckle]

197
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
[Killua snorts]

198
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
I guess these guys
specialize in hunting newbies.

199
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
This is what they do.

200
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Get wins beating us up.

201
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[Sadaso] We’re getting desperate here.

202
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
See, our deadline is approaching.

203
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
C’mon. We wanna fight. [light chuckle]

204
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
I’ll even demonstrate my power for you,

205
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
right here and now.

206
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
How about that?

207
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Okay. I’m gonna be fighting
on June the tenth.

208
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Hey! Gon!

209
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
That won’t work for me.

210
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:54,000
I’m sorry to tell you,
but my deadline is May 29th.

211
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Fight on that day.

212
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Who cares about your stupid deadline,
you idiot?

213
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Let’s get going.

214
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Gon, my friend…

215
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,000
You and I will fight.

216
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,000
I guarantee it. [light chuckle]

217
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
It’s a promise.

218
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[Killua] Come on. Ignore him.

219
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,000
What are you gonna do?

220
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
I’m going to force him to fight me.

221
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
[snickers]

222
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[Killua]
Visualize energy building up in your body.

223
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Feel the power from each
and every cell… gathering.

224
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Growing and growing…

225
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Then, all of a sudden,
force that power out!

226
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,000
[tired exhale]

227
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
I’m getting the hang of it!

228
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
The timing to get Ten
to contain that aura

229
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
was a little bit tricky.

230
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
[Zushi] Wait… a little?!

231
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
How are they picking it up so fast?

232
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
But Zushi’s aura is stronger.

233
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
We’re not even close to matching him yet.

234
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Guess we ought to train more.

235
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,000
[Zushi] Uh… N-no! That’s enough.

236
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Learning when to rest
is a big part of training.

237
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Why don’t we just call it a day.

238
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Really? Cause I ca--

239
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
I told you no!

240
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
If they surpass me in half a day,

241
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
I’ll lose all my motivation!

242
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
What’s the deal?

243
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Oh, it’s fine.

244
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
So more tomorrow?

245
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Works for me.

246
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,000
I’ll see you again tomorrow.

247
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Take it easy!

248
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
All right, then.

249
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
[elevator dings]

250
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
[light chuckle]

251
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,000
[smirks]

252
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
[gasps]

253
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,000
[straining]

254
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,000
[Zushi] I can’t--

255
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
I can’t…. move!

256
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:19,000
I can’t talk or breathe, either!

257
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,000
What’s going on?!

258
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Oops.

259
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,000
It’s your turn.

260
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,000
All right.

261
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
[Gido's prosthetic leg
tapping on the pavement]

262
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
[snickers]

263
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,000
[Killua] Knock it off.

264
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
I figured you might be up to something.

265
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
But forget the dirty tricks.

266
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
You want a fight, fine.

267
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Which day do you want?

268
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Oh, and don’t worry.
I’ll let you win, ok?

269
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Wait. How about I give all of you a win?

270
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Good enough?

271
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Once I get my win against you,

272
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
your friend Gon will be my next victim.

273
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
If you wanna fight Gon,

274
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
you’ll have to work around his schedule.

275
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Something tells me

276
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,000
you’ll be happy to.

277
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
In fact, I can guarantee it.

278
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
[Sadaso chuckling]

279
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
[Sadaso] Okay.

280
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
If the two of you are willing to fight,

281
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,000
it’ll save us the trouble
of using tactics like this one.

282
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:36,000
What do you say we all register together?

283
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Once that’s done,
we’ll return the boy unharmed.

284
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Yeah, sure. Okay.

285
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
But this is absolutely the very last time.
You got that?

286
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,000
There. May 29th.

287
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Done. You happy now?

288
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Yes.

289
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
We’ll return your friend here.

290
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
And up we go.

291
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Oh. I’ll say it again -

292
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
It’s the last time.

293
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
And if you break your promise…

294
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
[Killua sighs]

295
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Whatever.

296
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Forget it.

297
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
[Riehlvelt] What? I’m curious…

298
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
What’s going to happen
if we break our promise?

299
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
[Killua]
There’s no point in telling you now.

300
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Just keep your end of the deal, okay?

301
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[smirks]

302
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
[ringing]

303
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Hello? Is this Gon?

304
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
I don’t think I have to tell you
what this means.

305
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
As long as you don’t tell anyone

306
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
and you follow my instructions
to the letter,

307
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
the three of you will be able
to train tomorrow,

308
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,000
just like you planned.

309
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,000
[Gon] Zushi…

310
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
So how did it go with Gon?

311
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
[Gido] Perfectly.

312
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
He’s registered for the thirtieth.

313
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
[snickers] That makes two victories.

314
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Too easy.

315
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,000
[Sadaso cackling]

316
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Not killing people
is harder than I thought it’d be.

317
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Ah, man.

318
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Honest living is tough.

319
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
[scalper] Step right up!

320
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Get your tickets here!

321
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
These are hot off the presses,
ladies and gents!

322
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Gon versus Sadaso!

323
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,000
We’ve got Killua versus Sadaso, too!

324
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Better buy ‘em now
or you’re gonna regret it!

325
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
-[Killua] Hey pops.
-‘Sup, kid?

326
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,000
That Sadaso guy has just one arm?

327
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[scalper] That’s right!

328
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
The one-armed fighter
with a face like a mask.

329
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
If he grabs you
with his invisible left arm,

330
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,000
you’re done.

331
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
See… they call him
the newbie hunter and--

332
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,000
That son of a…

333
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
[Gon] Killua? Hey…

334
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Gon. This is where you’ve been?

335
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Uh… yeah…

336
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Killua.

337
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
I hear that you helped Zushi
home last night.

338
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Thank you.

339
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Are you feeling all right?

340
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Yeah. I’m fine.

341
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
I was probably just tired, that’s all.

342
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
I’m sorry to worry you!

343
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Oh. Hey, Mister Wing.

344
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Do you think that we can
watch that video again?

345
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Cause I figured out how to use Gyo.

346
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Huh?! Really?

347
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Fifteen threads, right?

348
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Thirteen for the cards,
one more for the scarf

349
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
and one well-hidden one
for the arm he tossed.

350
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
And then…

351
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Keep going.

352
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,000
Hisoka’s aura.

353
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
It almost looks like...

354
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
it’s expanding and contracting.

355
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Or does it attract certain objects

356
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
like a magnet does?

357
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
How else would his arm reattach itself?

358
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Not to mention flying off
and targeting Kastro’s jaw?

359
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,000
My money is on the former.

360
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,000
I think his aura must be stretchy,

361
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,000
like rubber or something.

362
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,000
And if it is,

363
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
then that would explain
most of his magic tricks.

364
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
He’s on a completely different level!

365
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
You pass. That’s very good.

366
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Although, I am a little surprised.

367
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:56,000
I certainly never expected both of you
to actually learn Gyo overnight.

368
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Both of us?

369
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Yep. But I still couldn’t figure out
what Hisoka’s ability was.

370
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
-[Zushi sighs]
-So, Killua,

371
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
I’m sure now
that you’ve finished your assignment,

372
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,000
you’ll be wanting to fight soon, correct?

373
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,000
It’s okay.

374
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
I didn’t mean to beat you to the punch.

375
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
I guess I just got
an itch to fight, that’s all.

376
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Yeah. I understand.

377
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
They must ‘a threatened you.

378
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Huh, Gon?

379
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Actually, I’ve already chosen
my day to fight.

380
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,000
I signed up for May 29th.

381
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
I’m fighting on May 30th.

382
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
All right, fine.

383
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
I guess I underestimated your progress.

384
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
It’s quite impressive.

385
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Between now and your scheduled fights

386
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
practice both Ten and Ren.

387
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
And in addition to your training,

388
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,000
get plenty of rest and sleep.

389
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,000
[Gon and Killua] Osu!

390
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
-[Gon] Killua.
-[Killua] Hm?

391
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,000
[Gon] Those guys threatened you, too,
didn’t they?

392
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
That makes me so mad…

393
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Yeah. But still…

394
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
my biggest concern
was getting Wing’s permission.

395
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
[Gon] I guess my biggest concern is

396
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
that they’ll do
the same thing to Zushi again.

397
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,000
[Killua] It’s okay.

398
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,000
You don't need to worry.

399
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,000
[Sadaso]
Today, I'll beat Killua for my sixth win.

400
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Tomorrow, I'll beat Gon
for my seventh win.

401
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
After that,

402
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
all I’ll need to do
is find three more suckers...

403
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
[chuckling]

404
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
...then I’ll be a Floor Master!

405
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,000
With the kind of fame and fortune
that’ll get me,

406
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,000
I’ll be set for the rest of my life!

407
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,000
[gasps]

408
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
[Killua] You move, you die.

409
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
You use Nen and you die.

410
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Make a sound and you die.

411
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
If you understand, close your eyes.

412
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Do you see what happens
when you break your promises?

413
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
If you do, open your eyes,

414
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,000
look at me in the mirror
and listen carefully.

415
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Don’t ever show your dirty face
in front of us again.

416
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,000
You’ll keep this promise.

417
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
[referee] Sadaso’s time is up!

418
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Killua wins by default!

419
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,000
[spectator] Are you kidding me?
What is this?

420
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
[disgruntled spectators shouting]

421
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:30,000
[narrator] Killua opens the battle
against the persistent trio

422
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,000
with a technical victory.

423
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Thanks to their unique natural talents,

424
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:39,000
the real battle at Heavens Arena
is only just beginning for Gon and Killua

425
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
who are learning Nen at incredible speed!

426
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[theme song playing]

427
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
[Gon] Coming up:

428
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

429
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

430
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

431
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

432
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Today, we’ll be introducing Sadaso!

433
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:08,000
He went through the traditional initiation
with Gido and Riehlvelt. [giggles]

434
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:11,000
One arm’s invisible
cause it’s made of Nen. [giggles]

435
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,000
That’s right!

436
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:19,000
[Gon] Next time: “Power To Avenge”!

437
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,000
Power… right?

438
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,000
[Killua] Avenge... right?

439
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Gon and Killua] Right? Right? Right?
